WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.793
Please welcome Captain Sarah Kociuba.

2
00:00:03.641 --> 00:00:05.824
Captain! Wow!

3
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:08.824
(audience applauds)

4
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.730
Hi, thanks for having me.

5
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.070
I'm very excited to be here.

6
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.620
I can't, like, how did it feel

7
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.410
when you got the phone call of,

8
00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.400
we would like you to be the first of a first

9
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.850
of a first to fly the bomber in the lead at the Super Bowl?

10
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.990 line:15%
Yes, it was very humbling and very exciting.

11
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.960 line:15%
So, we have a very strong group

12
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.370 line:15%
of B-2 instructor pilots here at Whiteman Air Force Base.

13
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.540
So, to be chosen just within that elite group

14
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.200
was very exciting and humbling.

15
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.780
And then, you know, on the actual flyover day itself,

16
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.450
on Sunday, as I stepped to my aircraft, you know,

17
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.170
the entire team was there supporting us,

18
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.440
getting the jet ready to go.

19
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.300
So the entire maintenance team and support team,

20
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.520
and I just felt such a great amount of pride

21
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.310
to be representing that entire team.

22
00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.210
And then the entire global strike team as well,

23
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.660
leading both the other two aircraft.

24
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.750
That's so cool.

25
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.250
And you think, 500 missions you've done in combat.

26
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.630
This is very different, right?

27
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.780
So when you're flying over the big game,

28
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.140
what's going through your mind?

29
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.530
Are you looking down to see if you can spot Tom Brady?

30
00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.187
What are you looking for?

31
00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.390
Admittedly, no, I was not looking for Tom Brady.

32
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.276
Maybe Mahomes, but -

33
00:01:19.276 --> 00:01:20.109
Girl, I understand.

34
00:01:20.109 --> 00:01:23.430
That's right, you're a big Kansas City Chiefs fan.

35
00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.450
Yeah. That's our home team here, absolutely.

36
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.984
That's right.

37
00:01:26.984 --> 00:01:28.820
So, we were supporting them, but yeah,

38
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.350
so really focus up until the last few seconds.

39
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.570 line:15%
Obviously, I was excited, but we were really focusing

40
00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.920 line:15%
on maintaining that tight formation and to make sure

41
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.010 line:15%
that we were going to be on time.

42
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.110
But then in those last 10 seconds,

43
00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.680
my ground controller keyed the mic

44
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.790
so we could really fine tune our timing.

45
00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.990
So I was able to hear the last few seconds

46
00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.720
of the National Anthem, and I have never felt such pride.

47
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.250
And it was really the pinnacle for my passion of flying

48
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.350
and, you know, my passion for America.

49
00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.550
And I felt like as we were pushing the throttles up there

50
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.330
in the last 10 seconds, that I was just saying,

51
00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.040
this is for you, America.

52
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.760
And then we flew over and I, it was just very exciting.

53
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.810
Now, Sarah, why does it look like

54
00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.970
you're in Batman's plane,

55
00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.350
and the one to your left

56
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.241
is like a Delta flight on its way to Vegas?

57
00:02:17.241 --> 00:02:18.357
Yeah, I know, totally.

58
00:02:18.357 --> 00:02:20.200
You're totally right.

59
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.300
Yeah, what's that about?

60
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.360
Yeah, so, the aircraft on our left is the B-52,

61
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.300
and that is our workhorse bomber.

62
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.560
She's been around for a long time.

63
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.290
She's our reliable bomber there, but yeah,

64
00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.500
we've got the stealth in the lead, the B-1 -

65
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.333
Yeah, there you go.

66
00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:37.166
Drop the mic.

67
00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:38.475
That's you.

68
00:02:38.475 --> 00:02:42.810
Do you have any advice, you know, right now for,

69
00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.230
I don't know, any woman who, like,

70
00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.483
may be stressing, out there in the world?

71
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.820
Yeah, absolutely.

72
00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.280
So, everybody gets stressed, right.

73
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.010 line:15%
But it's kind of two-fold how I manage my stress.

74
00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.500 line:15%
My sister is actually a neuropsychologist,

75
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.842 line:15%
so she has really hammered home

76
00:02:57.842 --> 00:03:01.390 line:15%
the importance of mindfulness in the day to day.

77
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:04.100 line:15%
So I try to practice that as much as I can

78
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.370 line:15%
and remind myself it's important,

79
00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.116 line:15%
but really in the execution phase, I maintain my calm,

80
00:03:09.116 --> 00:03:11.700 line:15%
just because of all the extensive training we do.

81
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.605
So, whether it's in the simulator or flying or studying

82
00:03:15.605 --> 00:03:18.200
or mission prepping and briefing,

83
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.510
we are constantly training.

84
00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.300
So, when I step to that aircraft and take off,

85
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.430
I really fall back on all the training that I have

86
00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.790
because, you know, we got to make decisions on the fly

87
00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:31.010
and we're going very fast.

88
00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.640
Decisions need to come in very fast.

89
00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.040
So, I just really fall back on that training.

90
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.450
Could I ever come get in the simulator sometime

91
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.900
to see what it's like?

92
00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.733
Yeah, absolutely.

93
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:41.566
Come out to Whiteman.

94
00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:43.553
We'll be, I will personally give you guys a tour

95
00:03:43.553 --> 00:03:45.360
of the jet and the simulator.

96
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.760
Come on over.

97
00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.790
Okay. Thank you.

98
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.740
Oh my God.

99
00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:50.878
Do you wanna go?

100
00:03:50.878 --> 00:03:53.200
Can I, I want to come.

101
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.033
Yeah, you can come.

102
00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.440
Okay. And I'll, like -

103
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.860
It's a little bit of security prep

104
00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.080
that we'll have to do beforehand, but -

105
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.570
Am I correct in this, Sarah that you,

106
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.620
when you were little, you went to Super Bowls

107
00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.640
and saw the planes fly over?

108
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.473
Close. Yeah.

109
00:04:07.473 --> 00:04:08.890
So my parents, I grew up in Cleveland,

110
00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.710
and they took us to the Cleveland Air Show

111
00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.080
pretty much every year.

112
00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.900
So, I got to see not only the static aircraft there,

113
00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.570
but all the aircraft fly,

114
00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.740 line:15%
and that's kind of where my passion kicked in,

115
00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:22.160 line:15%
just seeing the aircraft, hearing them, feeling it.

116
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:23.760 line:15%
And then when I was 11,

117
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.930 line:15%
my sister was marching in the Rose Bowl Parade,

118
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.680
so my parents took us out there.

119
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:28.760
So, yeah.

120
00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:29.593
That was it.

121
00:04:29.593 --> 00:04:33.740
Right when the parade starts, the B-2 does its fly over,

122
00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.760
and I had never seen anything like that in my life,

123
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.570
and I just thought it was the coolest thing as a kid.

124
00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:43.380
And it really stuck with me for the rest of my life.

125
00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.938
What do you say to little girls

126
00:04:45.938 --> 00:04:49.260
who may have the same dreams that you did

127
00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.590
and wanted to fly a plane one day?

128
00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.784
To any little girl or little boy out there

129
00:04:53.784 --> 00:04:57.330
that wants to fly, think aviation is cool,

130
00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.350
maybe has a passion for it, to just go chase your dreams.

131
00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.830
You know, we live in this great country

132
00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.502
where we're afforded the opportunity to go chase our dreams.

133
00:05:04.502 --> 00:05:06.330
So, go check it out.

134
00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:09.210
Get into the world of aviation. See if you like it.

135
00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.560
And you know, most importantly,

136
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.269
don't let anybody out there convince you

137
00:05:12.269 --> 00:05:13.760
that you can't do it.

138
00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.230
You are living proof of that.

139
00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.956
Thank you, Captain Sarah Kociuba.

140
00:05:18.956 --> 00:05:22.660
I am just so honored to meet you.

141
00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.983
Me, too. It's very exciting.

142
00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:28.388
Thank you! This is so awesome!

143
00:05:28.388 --> 00:05:30.971 line:15%
(upbeat music)

